invariant: INV-14
file: srv_flight.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: srv_select stops refusing a client whose ALPN list holds no name the
  caller offers, so the handshake completes with alpn_selected at
  CH_ALPN_NONE and EncryptedExtensions carries no ALPN extension. RFC 7301
  section 3.2 requires a fatal no_application_protocol alert there. The
  parser cannot catch this: srv_parser_ext.c reports the offer and reaches
  no verdict on it, and this function is the only place that reads the
  caller's list and the client's together. test/srv_flight_tests.h,
  test_flight_alpn, offers two protocols against a hello whose list missed
  both and requires alert 120.

--- old
    if (alpn_mismatch(&h->t->cfg, ch)) {
        h->alert = ALERT_NO_APPLICATION_PROTOCOL;
        return CH_EPROTO;
    }
--- new
    (void)alpn_mismatch(&h->t->cfg, ch);
